      "final_message": "`service2.compute_fee(1000, \"gold\")` returns **480**. Running it directly gave the same number.\n\n`compute_fee` only imports from `pricing.py` and `discounts.py`:\n1. **Base fee:** `pricing.base_fee(1000)` is `500 + 1000 // 10`, which is 600.\n2. **Discount:** `discounts.apply_discount(600, \"gold\")` takes off 20%: `600 - (600 * 20) // 100` is `600 - 120`, which is 480.\n\n`decoy_tax.py` and `decoy_shipping.py` are never imported, so they don't affect the result.\n\nANSWER: 480",
